-- Income Tax Ordinance [New Version], s 60A(b)(2): the assessment of a member of a renewed kibbutz on income he did not report to the kibbutz.
-- Quotations (`src:N`) are copied mechanically from line N of
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/income-tax-ordinance-new-version.he.wiki.txt (sha256 b87f2cf4...6b81b6).
--
-- WHAT IT SAYS. (b)(1) The assessment of a renewed kibbutz and of all its members is made, notwithstanding the Ordinance, under this section. (2)
-- Notwithstanding (1), the assessment of a member of a renewed kibbutz on income he did not report to the kibbutz is not made under this section, and in
-- it the rates and credit points counted in the kibbutz's assessment, and the kibbutz's losses, are not counted.
--
-- The same shape as s 55(b), and the same open question (NOTES.md, Q5). The rest of s 60A ((a) definitions, (b)(1), (3), (4), (c) and (d)) is not named
-- by the row and is not encoded (NOTES.md coverage table).

§ `Section 60A(b)(2) — the member of a renewed kibbutz`

-- src:1915 | (ב)(1) שומתם של קיבוץ מתחדש ושל כל חבריו תיעשה, על אף האמור בפקודה זו, לפי הוראות סעיף זה.
-- src:1916 | (2) על אף האמור בפסקה (1), שומתו של חבר קיבוץ מתחדש על הכנסה שלא דווחה על ידי החבר לקיבוץ, לא תיעשה לפי הוראות סעיף זה, ובשומה זו לא יובאו בחשבון שיעורי המס ונקודות הזיכוי אשר הובאו בחשבון בשומתו של הקיבוץ המתחדש וכן הפסדיו של הקיבוץ.

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 60A(b)(1)-(2) (source lines 1915-1916)
GIVEN `the income was reported to the kibbutz` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `How the income of a kibbutz member is assessed`
`s 60A(b) — the member's income is assessed` `the income was reported to the kibbutz` MEANS
    IF   `the income was reported to the kibbutz`
    THEN `under the sub-chapter on the kibbutz and its members`
    ELSE `apart from that sub-chapter, the rates and credit points counted in the kibbutz's assessment and the kibbutz's losses not being counted`

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 60A(b)(2) (source line 1916)
GIVEN `the income was reported to the kibbutz` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60A(b)(2) — the credit points counted in the kibbutz's assessment are left out of the member's assessment of income` `the income was reported to the kibbutz` MEANS
    NOT `the income was reported to the kibbutz`

